1
00:00:08,118 --> 00:00:10,578
Did the listing actually say "miniature"?

2
00:00:12,747 --> 00:00:14,587
(Leonard:)I just assumed.

3
00:00:15,167 --> 00:00:19,587
Well, who sells a full-sized time machine
for $800?

4
00:00:19,754 --> 00:00:22,424
(Sheldon:)In a Venn diagram,
that would be an individual located...

5
00:00:22,591 --> 00:00:25,431
(Sheldon:)...within the intersection of
"no longer want time machine"...

6
00:00:25,594 --> 00:00:28,264
...and "need $800."

7
00:00:28,847 --> 00:00:30,597
(Howard:)It's actually a tremendous bargain.

8
00:00:30,765 --> 00:00:35,015
(Howard:)Even with shipping,
it works out to less than $4 a pound.

9
00:00:35,187 --> 00:00:37,727
Cocktail shrimp are 12.50.

10
00:00:39,816 --> 00:00:42,486
How are we gonna get it upstairs?

11
00:00:43,111 --> 00:00:45,821
(Howard:)If we take the dish off,
it might fit in the elevator.

12
00:00:45,989 --> 00:00:48,489
(Leonard:)Yes, but the elevator's been broken
for two years.

13
00:00:48,658 --> 00:00:52,368
(Sheldon:)I've been meaning to ask you, do you think
we should make a call about that?

14
00:00:53,955 --> 00:00:56,795
(Howard:)Not necessary.
I have a Master's in engineering.

15
00:00:56,958 --> 00:00:59,838
(Howard:)I remotely repair satellites
on a regular basis.

16
00:01:00,003 --> 00:01:03,463
I troubleshoot space-shuttle payloads.

